{"id": "EUVD-2026-76631", "enisaUuid": "4b45bb1d-0049-3e48-a588-af652b472226", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nzram: fix out-of-bounds access in read_block_state()\n\nread_block_state() calculates nr_pages before taking dev_lock.  If the\ndevice is reset and reinitialized with a smaller disksize before lock\nacquisition, nr_pages still describes the old table.  The subsequent loop\ncan then call slot_lock() past the end of the newly allocated table.\n\nRead disksize after acquiring dev_lock and checking that the device is\ninitialized.  The read lock then keeps the table and its bound stable for\nthe duration of the scan.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:30", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5e9f3a75efc774f17ab3f33826630d7fe30c7ea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d52c1f43ff39ea1ebf8f016e847677f0b60cf2b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7dbcb7a561a21e9a8f5b5fa90bb95aefbd0739d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e458fa714a55b6b64a9fe0c6d4fa609609f9ec3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/391f057f44a51cc9418da5cba78b014324174264"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5pfc-pqwh-23px", "CVE-2026-89719"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03bf8f50-03e6-390f-a577-a6cf028ce1f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "42b835ce-892d-3f36-ab22-39004147231d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "489e22b3-ba9b-33c6-a2fc-296dace6fc0c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4e967c24-ffc5-318d-a8ad-c43a1d154745", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5bfe2ff2-bbb8-3864-bdd3-93a7be7c05ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c0265342bff4fcaa2cdf13f